Subject: [PATCH] tu/a8xx: reset LRZ control after flush

tu_lrz_tiling_end() enables LRZ control for the end-of-render-pass
FD_LRZ_FLUSH, but leaves the control registers set afterwards.

On A8xx and newer, reset GRAS_LRZ_CNTL and GRAS_LRZ_CNTL2 after the
flush using tu6_write_lrz_cntl(). Avoid leaving the flush control
state active when a subsequent render pass changes LRZ buffers.

This follows the GRAS control cleanup in freedreno's fd6_lrz_inv().
The change also covers sysmem render-pass end when
tu_lrz_sysmem_end() delegates to tu_lrz_tiling_end().

LRZ fast-clear remains enabled for use by subsequent render passes,
which program their LRZ state again. No explicit WFI or additional
LRZ flush is introduced.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc
index 1ae27c2475f..084fc5fa2f4 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc
@@ -929,6 +929,9 @@ tu_lrz_tiling_end(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd, struct tu_cs *cs)
    } else {
       tu_emit_event_write<CHIP>(cmd, cs, FD_LRZ_FLUSH);
    }
+
+   if (CHIP >= A8XX)
+      tu6_write_lrz_cntl<CHIP>(cmd, cs, {});
 }
 TU_GENX(tu_lrz_tiling_end);
 
